00108E  2               ; blit_title_char: like print_bitmap_line's per-character work, but for
00108E  2               ; one 3x2-cell (double-width AND double-height) title letter - double
00108E  2               ; width because a letter doubled in height only, not width, would be
00108E  2               ; distorted (tall and thin) rather than uniformly bigger. A = spfont
00108E  2               ; glyph code, temp3 = dest bitmap TOP-LEFT cell ptr, temp4 = dest
00108E  2               ; screen-matrix TOP-LEFT cell ptr, colour = plain 0-15 foreground value.
00108E  2               ; Each source row maps via TITLE_B0/B1/B2 (each of the glyph's 5 real
00108E  2               ; columns doubled to 2 color-pixels, matching the 2x vertical doubling -
00108E  2               ; 10 color-pixels of glyph + a 2-pixel gap = 12 = exactly 3 cells, no
00108E  2               ; remainder, so unlike body text this needs no sub-cell offset
00108E  2               ; alternation). Each row's 3 bytes are written twice (rows 0-3 into the
00108E  2               ; top cells, rows 4-7 into the bottom cells 320 bitmap-bytes / 40
00108E  2               ; screen-matrix-bytes below - one screen row down). Leaves temp3/temp4
00108E  2               ; pointing at the bottom-left cell on return; callers must recompute
00108E  2               ; fresh for the next letter, not rely on them afterward.
00108E  2               blit_title_char:
00108E  2  AA               tax
00108F  2  A9 00            lda #0
