0011BE  2               ; LEFT_TABLE/RIGHT_TABLE: indexed by a source glyph row's top 5 bits (its
0011BE  2               ; 5 real pixel columns, srcbyte>>3, giving an index 0-31), giving the
0011BE  2               ; left-half and right-half destination bytes for MULTICOLOR bitmap mode,
0011BE  2               ; for a letter starting at color-pixel offset 0 within its cell. Each of
0011BE  2               ; the 5 real source columns maps to exactly one 2-bit color-pixel (code
0011BE  2               ; 10 = screen-matrix low nibble = the text's foreground color; code 00 =
0011BE  2               ; background) at NATIVE width - no stretching. A cell holds 4 color-
0011BE  2               ; pixels (2 bits x 4 = 8 bits = the cell's 1 byte for that row): the left
0011BE  2               ; cell's 4 slots hold source columns 0-3, the right cell's first slot
0011BE  2               ; holds column 4, leaving that cell's last 3 slots for print_bitmap_line
0011BE  2               ; to fill with the NEXT letter (see LEFT_TABLE_2/RIGHT_TABLE_2 below) -
0011BE  2               ; true BBC letter spacing doesn't land on this table alone.
0011BE  2               LEFT_TABLE:
0011BE  2  00 00 02 02      .byte $00,$00,$02,$02,$08,$08,$0A,$0A
0011C2  2  08 08 0A 0A  
0011C6  2  20 20 22 22      .byte $20,$20,$22,$22,$28,$28,$2A,$2A
0011CA  2  28 28 2A 2A  
0011CE  2  80 80 82 82      .byte $80,$80,$82,$82,$88,$88,$8A,$8A
0011D2  2  88 88 8A 8A  
0011D6  2  A0 A0 A2 A2      .byte $A0,$A0,$A2,$A2,$A8,$A8,$AA,$AA
0011DA  2  A8 A8 AA AA  
0011DE  2               RIGHT_TABLE:
0011DE  2  00 80 00 80      .byte $00,$80,$00,$80,$00,$80,$00,$80
0011E2  2  00 80 00 80  
