0011FE  2               ; LEFT_TABLE_2/RIGHT_TABLE_2: same idea, for a letter starting at
0011FE  2               ; color-pixel offset 2 (the alternate case - see print_bitmap_line's
0011FE  2               ; comment on why offsets 0/2 alternate). LEFT_TABLE_2's slots 0-1 are
0011FE  2               ; always 0 (that cell's first 2 slots belong to the PREVIOUS letter,
0011FE  2               ; combined in via ORA, not this table) and source columns 0-1 land in
0011FE  2               ; its slots 2-3; RIGHT_TABLE_2 holds source columns 2-4 in slots 0-2,
0011FE  2               ; leaving slot 3 as this letter's 1-color-pixel trailing gap.
